      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "body": "<!-- \u26a0\ufe0f\u26a0\ufe0f Do Not Delete This! feature_request_template \u26a0\ufe0f\u26a0\ufe0f -->\n<!-- Please read our Rules of Conduct: https://opensource.microsoft.com/codeofconduct/ -->\n<!-- Please search existing issues to avoid creating duplicates. -->\n\nAdd an experimental setting for the Agents Window that initially places the provider-owned **Agent** picker in the **Add Context** menu for new and running session chat inputs.\n\nAfter the user explicitly selects an agent\u2014including the currently selected default\u2014the picker should return to its usual toolbar position for that session. The placement behavior should work independently of the experimental new-session composer layout.\n\nThis reduces persistent prompt chrome while keeping agent selection discoverable alongside other context actions.",
